# Database configuration

Where the coordinator's database is, from the environment its container is given:
`MACSAD_DATABASE_HOST`, `MACSAD_DATABASE_PORT`, `MACSAD_DATABASE_NAME`,
`MACSAD_DATABASE_USER`, and `MACSAD_DATABASE_PASSWORD_FILE`, the file holding the
password. The password is read from that file and never from the environment, so
it appears in no process listing and no crash report; the connection URL is built
in memory, used, and never printed. `MACSAD_DATABASE_TLS=require` makes the
connection refuse a server that will not encrypt, for a database across a network
the coordinator does not own.

This module checks the pieces; reading the environment and the file is the
caller's.

## Note
The password a secret file holds: its first line, without the line break a text
editor or `openssl rand -hex 32 > file` leaves after it.

## To passwordFromFile (content: Text) -> Text:
    Let first be item 1 of lines(content + "\n").
    Return trimEnd(first).

## Note
Whether a host name or address is safe to place in a URL: letters, digits, dots
and dashes, as a container network names a service.

## To isHostName (t: Text) -> Bool:
    If length of t is equal to 0 or length of t is greater than 253:
        Return false.
    Repeat for b in text_bytes(t):
        Let letter be (b is at least 97 and b is at most 122) or (b is at least 65 and b is at most 90).
        If (letter or (b is at least 48 and b is at most 57) or b is equal to 46 or b is equal to 45) is equal to false:
            Return false.
    Return true.

## Note
Whether a database or role name is a plain identifier: a letter or underscore,
then letters, digits and underscores, at most 63 bytes as PostgreSQL allows.

## To isSqlName (t: Text) -> Bool:
    If length of t is equal to 0 or length of t is greater than 63:
        Return false.
    Let mutable first be true.
    Repeat for b in text_bytes(t):
        Let word be (b is at least 97 and b is at most 122) or (b is at least 65 and b is at most 90) or b is equal to 95.
        If (word or (first is equal to false and b is at least 48 and b is at most 57)) is equal to false:
            Return false.
        Set first to false.
    Return true.

## Note
The connection URL, or what is wrong with the pieces. A password may hold any
byte but the ones that would end the URL's user part.

## To databaseUrl (host: Text, port: Int, name: Text, user: Text, password: Text) -> Result of Text and Text:
    If isHostName(host) is equal to false:
        Return a new Err with error "MACSAD_DATABASE_HOST is not a host name".
    If port is less than 1 or port is greater than 65535:
        Return a new Err with error "MACSAD_DATABASE_PORT is not a port".
    If isSqlName(name) is equal to false or isSqlName(user) is equal to false:
        Return a new Err with error "MACSAD_DATABASE_NAME and MACSAD_DATABASE_USER must be plain identifiers".
    If length of password is equal to 0 or password contains "@" or password contains "/":
        Return a new Err with error "the database password file is empty or holds @ or /".
    Return a new Ok with value "postgres://" + user + ":" + password + "@" + host + ":" + "{port}" + "/" + name.

## Note
Whether the TLS setting demands an encrypted connection. Only the exact word
`require` does; anything else connects in the clear, as on the internal network
of the compose stack.

## To requiresTls (setting: Text) -> Bool:
    Return trim(setting) is equal to "require".

## Test: database passwords come from the first line of their file

Expect that passwordFromFile("0123abcd\n") is equal to "0123abcd".
Expect that passwordFromFile("0123abcd\r\n") is equal to "0123abcd".
Expect that passwordFromFile("0123abcd") is equal to "0123abcd".
Expect that passwordFromFile("") is equal to "".

## Test: database URLs are built only from checked pieces

Inspect databaseUrl("postgres", 5432, "macsad", "macsad_runtime", "ab12"):
    When Ok (u):
        Expect that u is equal to "postgres://macsad_runtime:ab12@postgres:5432/macsad".
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "built".
Inspect databaseUrl("postgres", 5432, "mac sad", "macsad_runtime", "ab12"):
    When Ok (u):
        Expect that u is equal to "refused".
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e contains "plain identifiers".
Expect that isHostName("172.17.0.2") is equal to true.
Expect that isHostName("db/evil") is equal to false.
Expect that isSqlName("1abc") is equal to false.

## Test: database TLS is required only when asked

For all booleans asked:
    Let mutable setting be "".
    If asked:
        Set setting to "require".
    Expect that requiresTls(setting) is equal to asked.
